Characterize a material by independent structural, optical, and chemical evidence (@mp-crystal-project: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @mineralogy-and-petrology, #source "../sources/Crystallography-Open-Database.lingua#r_0GWYXPDY9KYA4V4AXPCEFJG9RG", #source "../sources/GSAS-II-Refinement-Tutorials.lingua#r_14B5VSDN6YR5MQJVNTKYJXF3XB", #source "../sources/NIST-Quantitative-EDS.lingua#r_7XJDCAH01NX65F6Q5YY3CBFTCF", #source "../sources/Raman-Mineral-Identification-Practical-Guide.lingua#r_3TQHZH1T2CDCQPTVVXSKJ5DCED", #source "../sources/IUCr-Crystallographic-Teaching.lingua#r_334MQS5KEVRJ17XKK0WKCP6KWX", #mineralogy-and-petrology "Advanced-igneous-process-and-experimental-study.lingua#r_6TQ5TWWMJ8WZWXWBJTABAY0CQK") { r_5C4Q9327N8YT8SAN6Q8F2SJF1P
**Read:** [Crystallography Open Database — structures, citations, and CIF records](../sources/Crystallography-Open-Database.lingua#r_0GWYXPDY9KYA4V4AXPCEFJG9RG), the full selected structure record and original paper; [GSAS-II — diffraction analysis and refinement tutorials](../sources/GSAS-II-Refinement-Tutorials.lingua#r_14B5VSDN6YR5MQJVNTKYJXF3XB), all relevant complete tutorials and method references; [Electron-excited X-ray microanalysis by EDS at 50 — Newbury and Ritchie](../sources/NIST-Quantitative-EDS.lingua#r_7XJDCAH01NX65F6Q5YY3CBFTCF), the entire paper; [Raman Spectroscopy for Mineral Identification — Bartholomew and Post](../sources/Raman-Mineral-Identification-Practical-Guide.lingua#r_3TQHZH1T2CDCQPTVVXSKJ5DCED), the whole guide with the exact relevant method sections; [Crystallographic teaching pamphlets — IUCr](../sources/IUCr-Crystallographic-Teaching.lingua#r_334MQS5KEVRJ17XKK0WKCP6KWX), the full relevant crystallographic pamphlets.

Choose a bounded mineral/material question with authorized data and sufficient specimen/domain context. Read the full original structural and analytical papers, complete relevant GSAS-II tutorials, and the entire method guides. Actual instrument collection should use suitable supervised facilities; a supplied-data study must state that scope.

Connect hand/optical observations, composition, diffraction, and a structural model. Preserve preparation, instrument conditions, calibration/standards, raw/processed stages, versions, sampling support, and uncertainty. Test whether methods observed the same phase/domain or different mixtures.

Independently reproduce a consequential formula, spacing/cell, density, phase proportion, or spectral result. Compare a plausible polymorph, mixed-phase, occupancy, or redox account. Check geometric, component/site/charge, and instrumental constraints without treating a low fit residual as full identification.

**Work:** publish a research-style characterization account in your study workspace, with complete primary-source references, original calculations, independent checks, alternative model, limitations, and an appropriate next experiment. Ask another reader to reconstruct selected conclusions from the retained evidence and revise after substantive critique.

The result should explain what is identified, what is only constrained, and which uncertainty matters to a geological or material-use question. It should not claim every species/property from a single normalized analysis or a successful database match.

**Continue:** [Defend an igneous history using phase relations, material balance, and independent evidence](Advanced-igneous-process-and-experimental-study.lingua#r_6TQ5TWWMJ8WZWXWBJTABAY0CQK).

